Package: agora
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Agora desktop environment - runtime
 Agora is a desktop environment for Linux and the BSDs, built entirely from
 source. It is a Cocoa-compatible stack - Core Foundation, Foundation, Core
 Graphics, Core Text and the Application Kit, implemented in Objective-C -
 together with a Wayland window server that composites client-side window
 chrome, and the Workspace shell that draws the desktop, its menu bar, dock,
 icons and file windows.
 .
 The stack targets behavioural and API compatibility, so a program written
 against the documented Cocoa surface builds and runs against Agora without
 modification, and the desktop follows Mac OS X's window management rather
 than a Linux desktop's.
 .
 This package contains the shared libraries and the programs that make up a
 session: the window server and the Workspace shell.

Package: agora-dev
Architecture: any
Section: libdevel
Depends: agora (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Agora desktop environment - development files
 Headers, CMake package configuration files and pkg-config metadata for
 building C and Objective-C programs against the Agora stack: Core
 Foundation, Foundation, Core Graphics, Core Text, the Application Kit, Icon
 Services, Launch Services and the file-system watch service, together with
 the window server's client protocol.
 .
 The libraries are installed as shared objects and are versioned normally, so
 a program built against them needs no Agora-specific build tooling; CMake
 finds each component with find_package(<Component> CONFIG).
